`ctx` times out before `slowCall` finishes. What happens to the goroutine?

```go
func fetch(ctx context.Context) (string, error) {
    ch := make(chan string)
    go func() { ch <- slowCall() }()
    select {
    case v := <-ch:
        return v, nil
    case <-ctx.Done():
        return "", ctx.Err()
    }
}
```

1,000 goroutines call `c.Inc()` on the same `c`, and all finish. What is `c.n`?

```go
type Counter struct {
    mu sync.Mutex
    n  int
}

func (c Counter) Inc() {
    c.mu.Lock()
    defer c.mu.Unlock()
    c.n++
}
```

